%% UML sequence — two officers co-edit a draft, then both press Publish (as built)
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor A as Officer A (Web App)
  actor B as Officer B (Web App)
  participant CO as Collaboration (K-COLLAB)
  participant PO as Audience Policy (K-POLICY)
  participant DB as SQLite (C-DB)
  A->>CO: connect /ws/drafts/42, auth {token}
  CO->>PO: get_editable_draft(A, 42)
  PO-->>CO: collaborator and officer
  A->>CO: sync {state_vector}
  CO->>DB: load ydoc, version 16
  CO-->>A: sync {update, state_vector, version: 16}
  B->>CO: connect, auth, sync (same checks)
  CO-->>A: presence [A, B]
  par concurrent edits
    A->>CO: update {update}
    CO->>PO: may A still edit?
    CO->>DB: merge and save, version 17 (room lock)
    CO-->>A: ack {version: 17}
    CO->>PO: may B still edit?
    CO-->>B: update {update, version: 17}
  and
    B->>CO: update {update}
    CO->>DB: merge and save, version 18 (room lock)
    CO-->>B: ack {version: 18}
    CO-->>A: update {update, version: 18}
  end
  Note over A,B: Yjs merges are order-independent: both documents are equal and no text is lost
  opt B's connection drops
    Note over B: "Offline", edits stay in B's document
    B->>CO: reconnect, auth, sync {state_vector}
    CO-->>B: sync {what B misses, server state_vector}
    B->>CO: update {what the server misses}
  end
  par both press Publish
    A->>CO: POST /drafts/42/publish {expected_version: 18}
  and
    B->>CO: POST /drafts/42/publish {expected_version: 18}
  end
  CO->>DB: UPDATE draft SET status='published' WHERE id=42 AND version=18 AND status='editing'
  DB-->>CO: 1 row (A)
  CO->>DB: INSERT post with sanitized HTML, COMMIT
  CO-->>A: 201 post
  DB-->>CO: 0 rows (B)
  CO-->>B: 409 ALREADY_PUBLISHED {post_id}
  CO-->>B: published {post_id}, close 4409
